--TEST--
`Core\Command::run` answers a word no `decimal` reads with a usage status and runs no handler, rather than with a plausible zero — ADR 0086 § 6, ADR 0095
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The other side of the conversion, and the side that decides whether it is
// worth having: a command line is *input*, so a word the parameter's type does
// not read is a usage error and never a throw — § 6's own answer for a command
// line the table cannot fill. The two wrong answers are a zero the handler
// cannot tell from a written one and a `1.2` taken off the front of the word,
// which is the repair ADR 0095 refuses generally.
//
// The usage page itself goes to standard error (`Core\Command::run`'s own doc
// owns why), so what a case sees on stdout is the status and the silence where
// the handler would have written.
class Ledger {
    #[Core\Command(name: "deposit", about: "Add to the balance")]
    public static function deposit(decimal $amount): uint {
        echo "deposit ran, and nothing on this command line selected it\n";
        return 0;
    }
}

echo "status: ", Core\Command::run(), "\n";
echo "still running", "\n";
--ARGS--
deposit
1.2.3
--EXPECT--
status: 2
still running
